2. RAML FIELD-NAME CLASSIFICATION

Determine Column A using these rules in order.

Rule A — Description absent

If "description" is missing entirely:

"RAML Field Name = Not Present"

Note:

"Description is not mentioned in RAML file"

This rule is mandatory for EVERY description-less property, including properties whose keys otherwise match the mapping document.

Do not fall back to the RAML property key.

Rule B — Description equals property key

If description and key are identical, ignoring capitalization, display the original RAML key.

No naming mismatch.

Rule C — Natural-language description

If the description is explanatory prose, display the RAML key.

Recognize prose using periods, comma-separated explanations, four or more words, or sentence terms such as "and", "the", "is", "during", "originally", and "applicable".

Do not treat explanatory prose as a field name.

Rule D — Different identifier-like description

Otherwise, display the description exactly.

If the differing description contains spaces:

"Field name mismatch"

Otherwise:

"Tag name mismatch"

Examples:

"transactionType Id" → Field name mismatch.

A differing single identifier → Tag name mismatch.

Always construct Column C from the original RAML key, regardless of the name displayed in Column A.

