3. DATATYPE COMPARISON

Use two separate representations:

1. RAW datatype for Excel display.
2. NORMALIZED datatype for comparison.

Never overwrite raw display values with normalized values, except for the explicit legacy overrides in Section 7.

Apply these comparison equivalences:

RAML| Mapping| Comparison
date-only| date| MATCH
time-only| time| MATCH
int| integer| MATCH
number| double| MATCH
string| String| MATCH
boolean| Boolean| MATCH

Trim whitespace and ignore datatype capitalization for comparison only.

CRITICAL: "number" and "double" are equivalent.

A field must NOT fail solely because one source specifies "number" and the other specifies "double".

Likewise, equivalent date/time/integer representations must not produce datatype failures.

Other genuinely different types must fail.

If one source lacks a datatype, report the missing datatype explicitly.

Excel Columns E and F must preserve raw source spelling, capitalization, and leading/trailing spaces, except for Section 7 overrides.

