6. VALIDATION LOGIC

Evaluate these independent checks:

1. Path equality.
2. Field-name/description equality.
3. Normalized datatype equality.
4. Missing datatype.
5. Mandatory/Optional equality.

Overall Result:

"FAIL" if any applicable check fails.

Otherwise:

"PASS".

For mandatory comparison, internally convert RAML boolean to Mandatory/Optional.

If mapping mandatory status is "Not present", do not invent a mandatory mismatch. Apply the relevant missing-metadata or special-case rule.

Do not fail a row solely because its two datatype labels are equivalent under Section 3.

Notes

Generate only applicable discrepancy descriptions.

Use these exact phrases:

Condition| Note
Missing RAML description| Description is not mentioned in RAML file
Different identifier-like description| Tag name mismatch
Different name containing spaces| Field name mismatch
Standalone datatype mismatch| Data Type mismatch
Datatype mismatch combined with another issue| Datatype mismatch
Mandatory mismatch| Mandatory/Optional parameter mismatch
Missing mapping datatype| Data type missing from mapping document
Missing RAML datatype| Data type missing from RAML file
Missing mapping counterpart| Not present in mapping document
Missing RAML counterpart| Not present in RAML file

For combined issues, join descriptions with "and".

Default ordering:

Name → Datatype → Mandatory/Optional.

Apply the explicit courtesy-car exception in Section 7.

A fully passing row has blank Notes/Comments unless an explicit SME comment is required.

Do not produce datatype mismatch notes for "number" versus "double".

